# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.freeze() suspends all strands under that tag; the strand stays
#         frozen until t2.stop() terminates the outer scope.
# blocked: a chunk-top `,` group cannot share a declaration with its
#          arms.  t.freeze() / t.unfreeze() work from script (probed), but
#          the fixture needs the frozen strand and its observer in one
#          program, which means `;` before `,` -- and the parser refuses
#          to mix the two in one group.  Freeze semantics are covered in C
#          by tests/rt/test_sched.c::block_and_freeze_are_independent.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: tag-freeze
#
# Reason:
#   tag.freeze() requires two M4/M5 features: (1) method dispatch on a UTag
#   value (M4), and (2) the SUSPENDED strand-state machinery that actually
#   halts instruction dispatch for tagged strands (M5).  The ',' separator for
#   concurrent "freeze vs echo" observation also requires the M5 chk driver.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M5 with freeze/unfreeze machinery):
# # var t1 = Tag.new() | {};
# # var t2 = Tag.new() | {};
# # t2: { t1: t1.freeze(); echo("You don't see me") }, sleep(1s);
# # echo("I am the only one");
# # [00000001] *** I am the only one
# # t2.stop();
